# Cross-check at concurrency 2: `bench run` vs `vllm bench serve`

Generated by `bench verify` from the committed files; do not edit by hand.
Regenerate from the repository root (`make build` puts `bench` in `bin/`):

```sh
bench verify --vllm vllm a/run b/run
```

**Valid:** every side prefilled its prompts' unique part (engine-side check below).

| Metric | ours (a) | ours (b) | vLLM reported | vLLM recomputed | Δ ours (a) | Δ ours (b) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| TTFT p50 (ms) | 15.00 | 15.00 | 16.00 | 15.62 | -4.00% | -4.00% |
| TTFT p95 (ms) | 25.00 | 25.00 | 30.00 | 31.25 | -20.00% | -20.00% |
| TTFT p99 (ms) | 25.00 | 25.00 | 31.00 | 31.25 | -20.00% | -20.00% |
| TPOT p50 (ms) | 5.000 | 5.000 | 12.000 | 4.395 | +13.78% | +13.78% |
| TPOT p99 (ms) | 19.500 | 19.500 | 19.500 | 19.531 | -0.16% | -0.16% |
| E2E p50 (ms) | 25.0 | 25.0 | 27.0 | 27.3 | -8.57% | -8.57% |
| E2E p99 (ms) | 32.0 | 32.0 | 31.2 | 31.2 | +2.40% | +2.40% |
| RPS | 1.500 | 1.500 | 1.500 | 2.000 | -25.00% | -25.00% |
| Output tok/s | 3.5 | 3.5 | 3.0 | 3.0 | +16.67% | +16.67% |
| Mean output tokens | 4.00 | 4.00 | 2.00 | 2.00 | +100.00% | +100.00% |
| n | 4 | 4 | 3 | 3 |  |  |

- vLLM reported: its own figures, numpy-interpolated percentiles. vLLM recomputed: its per-request data with our nearest-rank method (TTFT = ttft; E2E = ttft + Σ itl; TPOT = Σ itl / (output_len − 1), output_len ≥ 2 only). Δ is ours against vLLM recomputed.
- RPS: vLLM recomputed is its steady-state rate (below), since ours excludes ramp-up by warmup; vLLM reported is completed / duration. Output tok/s is over vLLM's whole duration in both vLLM columns.
- Recomputation check, mean recomputed vs reported: TTFT 18.229 vs 18.229 ms (+0.0000%), TPOT 11.963 vs 11.963 ms (+0.0000%), E2E 27.669 vs 27.500 ms (+0.6155%).

## vLLM start burst

vLLM's measured run opens with all 2 requests sent at once. Without the first 2 by send time, its TTFT p50 / p95 / p99 is 7.81 / 7.81 / 7.81 ms (n = 1, nearest-rank). Our warmup absorbs the burst before the window opens.

## Steady-state RPS

vLLM's sends from first + 0 s to last − 0 s: 4 sends over 1.500 s, (n − 1) / span = **2.000 req/s**. Its overall request_throughput, ramp-up and drain included, is 1.500 req/s; ours against it: ours (a) +0.00%, ours (b) +0.00%.

## Engine-side check

From each side's `vllm_metrics.csv`: uncached prompt tokens per request = Δ(prefix_cache_queries − prefix_cache_hits) / Δ ttft_count, and engine mean TTFT = Δ ttft_sum / Δ ttft_count. Ours spans the samples covering the measured window; vLLM's, the whole file. A side is invalid below 0.9 × its prompts' unique part: an uncached prompt prefills at least its unique part, a cached one about 1 token.

| Side | Span | Seconds | TTFT count | Uncached tokens / request | Unique part | Engine mean TTFT (ms) | Status |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| ours (a) | measured window | 60.000 | 60 | 110.0 | 100 | 31.25 | ok |
| ours (b) | measured window | 60.000 | 60 | 110.0 | 100 | 31.25 | ok |
| vLLM | whole file | 61.000 | 16 | 100.0 | 100 | 31.25 | ok |
